# Nothing here belongs in an image.
#
# `node_modules` above all: the `dev` stage installs its own, and a host copy
# arriving via `COPY . .` would shadow it with a macOS build — which is the exact
# failure the anonymous `/app/node_modules` volume in docker-compose.yml exists to
# work around. Keeping it out of the context makes that belt-and-braces rather
# than load-bearing.
node_modules

# Build and test output. The `build` stage regenerates `dist`; the rest is only
# ever written by a run that is already over.
dist
playwright-report
test-results
.vite

# Anything environment-shaped. `VITE_API_BASE` defaults to `/api` in the source,
# and that default is the one a deployment wants — the SPA and the API share an
# origin through nginx. A stray `.env` on the build machine silently re-pointing
# the bundle at `http://localhost:8000` is a deployment that works on the machine
# that built it and nowhere else.
.env
.env.*
*.local
